                  {"id":"OKC-234","title":"Set a document title per route so
                  browser tabs and history show the current
                  page","project":"v0.1","team":"Open Knowledge
                  Compute","assignee":"Viktor Renkema","status":"In
                  Progress","description":"<linear-image>{\"type\":\"image\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"https://uploads.linear.app/50de2a5a-2a95-4645-94fd-d6a6434bcc9b/57d63795-7094-45a2-a666-9824321148d0/b164a860-6e64-4619-b64e-c18ec7a72f52?signature=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJwYXRoIjoiLzUwZGUyYTVhLTJhOTUtNDY0NS05NGZkLWQ2YTY0MzRiY2M5Yi81N2Q2Mzc5NS03MDk0LTQ1YTItYTY2Ni05ODI0MzIxMTQ4ZDAvYjE2NGE4NjAtNmU2NC00NjE5LWI2NGUtYzE4ZWM3YTcyZjUyIiwiaWF0IjoxNzkzODc4OTI1LCJleHAiOjE3OTM4NzkyMjV9.a70rYuyM8KO4KVuyPb28fEcq0QkbI09KxV4tfO0t2EM\",\"title\":\"CleanShot
                  2026-11-05 at
                  12.04.21@2x.png\",\"width\":990,\"height\":1046}}</linear-image>\n\n**Description**\n\n###
                  Problem\n\nEvery page in the web app has the same document
                  title, \"GitBook Knowledge\". It comes from the static
                  `<title>` in `packages/web/index.html` and never changes on
                  navigation. As a result:\n\n* Browser tabs all read \"GitBook
                  Knowledge\", so several open tabs look the same.\n* The
                  back-button history and the full history list show identical
                  entries, so you can't tell which settings page, repository or
                  conversation you were on.\n* Bookmarks, the Electron window
                  title and the macOS Window menu carry no page context.\n*
                  Screen reader users hear no page name when the route changes.
                  This fails WCAG 2.4.2 Page Titled (Level A).\n\n###
                  Expected\n\nEach route sets a unique, descriptive document
                  title, written as a breadcrumb from general to specific and
                  joined with `›`, as Linear does. The favicon carries the
                  brand, so the product name only shows where a route names
                  nothing more specific:\n\n* `Settings › Members`\n* `Settings
                  › Profile`\n* `<repository> › <file name>`\n* `<repository> ›
                  Review › Changes`\n* Fallback: `GitBook Knowledge`\n\n###
                  Recommended approach\n\nTanStack Router has built-in document
                  head management. Each route declares a `head` option that
                  returns a `title`, and `<HeadContent />` in the root component
                  writes it to the document. A nested route's title replaces its
                  parent's. That means the root route sets the fallback and each
                  leaf route sets its own title. The routes have no loaders, so
                  the titles come from URL params: a conversation reads
                  `<repository> › Conversation`. Live names (conversation title,
                  the repository's display title) are a follow-up.\n\nAcceptance
                  criteria\n\n* Every route has a title that names its page.
                  Only the home screen shows just \"GitBook Knowledge\".\n*
                  Titles update on client-side navigation, including back and
                  forward.\n* The Electron window title follows the same
                  title.\n\n### References\n\n* [WCAG 2.2: Understanding 2.4.2
                  Page
                  Titled](<https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/page-titled.html>)\n*
                  [W3C technique G88: Providing descriptive
                  titles](<https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Techniques/general/G88>)\n*
                  [MDN: the `<title>`
                  element](<https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/title>)\n*
                  [TanStack Router: Document head
                  management](<https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/document-head-management>)\n\n>>>
                  Agent notes\n\n* The static titles are in
                  `packages/web/index.html:8` and
                  `packages/app/src/renderer/index.html:6`. There is no `head`
                  option or `<HeadContent />` in `packages/web/src` yet.\n*
                  `@tanstack/react-router` ^1.170 supports `head: () => ({ meta:
                  [{ title }] })` on each route.\n* Build titles in one helper,
                  for example `formatDocumentTitle(...parts)`, so the separator
                  and product suffix are defined in one place.\n* Electron's
                  `BrowserWindow` follows `document.title` by default unless
                  something prevents the `page-title-updated` event. Check this
                  in
                  `packages/app`.\n\n>>>","createdAt":"2026-11-05T11:20:36.219Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-05T17:35:09.879Z","cycleId":null}
